From dabf5552b439a275550cda4ab16d030d87580f54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:15:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): hand a refused kanban notice back to the chat's
 owning backend [daveey]

A chat open in two backends polls its kanban notices in both. The non-owner claimed the
cursor, its turn was refused (SESSION_NOT_OWNED), and the batch was dropped, so the owner
never saw the completion (a parent missed its child's 'invite minted, not sent' handoff).
A refused or failed turn now rewinds its claims (CAS via rewind_notify_cursor) and backs
off claiming; the owner re-claims and delivers. Partially delivered claims stay buffered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
